
Gmail-style email + lead dashboard, rebuilt as LeadMaster.
Theme: Dark Gray + White Light (#2B2B2B / #FFFFFF / #FAFAFA / #D9D9D9 / #6E6E6E).
No pure black, no other colors. No print button. No mock, demo or fakes elements or comnponents.

1. What This Is
LeadMaster is a single-page dashboard that looks and behaves like Gmail, but is built around leads / people / organizations, not just mail.

Left: Sidebar + Compose
Center: Main view (Inbox / Sent / Outbox / Deleted / Assistant / Automation / Templates / Scheduled / Settings / Compose)
Right: Right Panel — Contacts / Calendar Reminders / Notes
Top: Header with search, Refresh, Simulate Error, People strip, Settings toggle
All state is saved in the app's deployment database (records API), not in browser storage.

2. Sidebar — Exactly 9 Features (In Order)
#	Feature	What It Does
1	Inbox	Multi-tab inbox: Primary / Promotions / Social / Updates / Forums. Each subtab has distinct emails + unread counts. List + Preview + Detail.
2	Sent	Sent emails, with Sent time. Same list / preview / detail pattern as Inbox.
3	Outbox	Queued / Sending / Failed emails. Actions: Resend, Cancel, Send All Now.
4	Deleted	Trashed emails. Actions: Restore, Delete Forever, Empty Trash.
5	Assistant	Summarize Inbox, Draft Reply Suggestions (Use Draft → Compose), Smart Cleanup, People to Follow Up / Priority Leads.
6	Automation	Rules: Auto-label invoices, Auto-star from boss, Auto-archive newsletters, Auto-move leads. Working on/off toggles. Add Rule form: Name + When (sender/subject contains) + Do (label / star / archive / move).
7	Templates	Grid: Welcome, Follow-up, Meeting Invite, Invoice Reminder, Thank You, Lead Nurture. Actions: Use Template (→ Compose pre-filled), Edit, Duplicate, Delete, New Template (Name / Subject / Body).
8	Scheduled	Send-later emails with date/time. Actions: Edit Schedule, Send Now, Cancel.
9	Settings	Profile + Signature, Theme (Dark Gray + White Light, fixed selected), Density Comfortable / Compact, Notifications, Default Reply, Vacation Responder, Signature Editor, Components Organizer (see §4), Save Settings.
Compose is a single specific option above Inbox in the sidebar. It is the ONLY compose entry point. No popup, no header Compose button, no duplicate. Sender Profile “Send Email”, Template “Use Template”, Assistant “Use Draft” all open this same dedicated Compose view, pre-filled.

